 ],
 "text": "Anthropic just gave agent skills away. 70 plus AI tools now run the same skill files. Over 1 million skills, nearly 280 million installs. Here's why that's huge. A skill is a saved how-to your AI can actually run. Write it once, use it in Claude, ChatGBT, or Cursor. No more pacing the same prompt every morning. So here are the five I'd set up first. 1. Inbox triage. It sorts what needs you from what doesn't. 2. Meeting notes. Every call becomes a task list. 3. The weekly report. It pulls the numbers and drafts it. 4. Research brief. One question in, sources out. 5. The daily brief. What's late? What's stuck? What needs you? And every one of them waits for my yes before it sends. Comment AI and I'll send you my starter pack plus the permission sheet."
